  "text_md": "## Display Font (Font Type=3):\n\n**Display PFD Definition Font**\n\n|Font number|........:|1|\n|---|---|---|\n|Font type|.........:|3|\n|Code page|.........:|T1D0BASE|\n|Font character set..... :||C0D0DB10|\n|Point size.........:||*NONE|\n|Text............:||GOTHIC ROMAN BOLD 10 POINTS|\n\nCode page and font character set\n\nPress Enter to continue. F3=Exit F12=Cancel\n\nThis display shows the definition of a type 3 font.\n\nThe following table explains the Display Source Overlay Font display and the Display PFD Definition Font display.\n\n|Field Name|Description|\n|---|---|\n|Font number|Shows the font number.|\n|Font type|Shows the font type (Code page and font character set)|\n|Code page|Shows the code page name.|\n|Font character set|Shows the font character set name.|\n|Point size|Shows the point size.|\n|Text|Shows the description of the font.|\n\n# 9=Set Initial Font\n\nTo change the definition of a font to the initial values, do the following on the Work with Source Overlay Fonts display or the Work with PFD Definition Fonts display.\n\n1. Type 9 in the *Opt.* column beside the font number for which you want to change the definition.\n2. Press Enter.\nAFP Utilities for iSeries: User’s Guide\n",
